{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are triaging a production checkout incident from offline evidence.\n\nInputs:\n- <SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/in/topology.json\n- <SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\n- <SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log\n- <SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log\n- <SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\n- <SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/in/logs/orders-db.log\n\nCreate exactly these output files:\n- <SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/out/root_cause.json\n- <SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n\nroot_cause.json requirements:\n- Top-level object with: incident_id, root_cause_service, root_cause_change_id, confidence, affected_services, evidence, excluded_red_herrings, recommended_next_steps.\n- evidence must be a list of objects with source_file and observation.\n- excluded_red_herrings must name misleading signals and why they are not the primary cause.\n\ntriage_notes.md requirements:\n- Summarize the dependency path from user impact to root cause.\n- Cite at least three fixture files by path.\n- Include immediate mitigation and verification steps.\n- Explicitly mark inferences vs directly observed facts.\n\nDo not modify input files. Do not use live services or external APIs.\n"}],"timestamp":1788159000872},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning evidence triage workflow**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0449d91e01a5cb75016a95241ae47487d2a3e0df5961f90a23\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning evidence triage workflow**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5hQHOtONw0s9QjjOcKKr7qmG|fc_0449d91e01a5cb75016a95241cfbf087d29ef398f8cbf7fde7","name":"workflow","arguments":{"action":"list"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":13969,"output":112,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":93,"totalTokens":14081,"cost":{"input":0.0027938000000000004,"output":0.0001344,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0029282}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788159000878,"responseId":"resp_0449d91e01a5cb75016a952419b78c87d2b1b9efae0dcd1c24","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5hQHOtONw0s9QjjOcKKr7qmG|fc_0449d91e01a5cb75016a95241cfbf087d29ef398f8cbf7fde7","toolName":"workflow","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"list\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"adversarial-verification\",\n      \"description\": \"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"task\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"verifier_count\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_repairs\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"accept_mean\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"reask_limit\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"classify-and-act\",\n      \"description\": \"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"categories\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"confidence_threshold\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"fan-out-and-synthesize\",\n      \"description\": \"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_branches\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"generate-and-filter\",\n      \"description\": \"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_candidates\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"shortlist_size\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"use_judge\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"goal\",\n      \"description\": \"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"objective\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_turns\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"loop-until-done\",\n      \"description\": \"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_iterations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_scoring\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_repeats\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"open-claude-design\",\n      \"description\": \"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"discover_references\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ralph\",\n      \"description\": \"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_loops\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tournament\",\n      \"description\": \"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_attempts\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"n_evaluations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"pivots\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"seed\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"models\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"action":"list","items":[{"name":"adversarial-verification","description":"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.","inputs":[{"name":"task","required":true},{"name":"verifier_count","required":false},{"name":"max_repairs","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"accept_mean","required":false},{"name":"reask_limit","required":false}]},{"name":"classify-and-act","description":"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"categories","required":false},{"name":"confidence_threshold","required":false}]},{"name":"fan-out-and-synthesize","description":"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_branches","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"generate-and-filter","description":"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_candidates","required":false},{"name":"shortlist_size","required":false},{"name":"use_judge","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"goal","description":"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"objective","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_turns","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"loop-until-done","description":"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_iterations","required":false},{"name":"progress_scoring","required":false},{"name":"progress_repeats","required":false}]},{"name":"open-claude-design","description":"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"discover_references","required":false}]},{"name":"ralph","description":"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_loops","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"tournament","description":"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_attempts","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false},{"name":"n_evaluations","required":false},{"name":"pivots","required":false},{"name":"seed","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"models","required":false}]}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788159005381},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning file generation workflow with fan-out**\n\n**Performing preworkflow file reconnaissance**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0449d91e01a5cb75016a95241e347087d2be3950147de9d5d5\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning file generation workflow with fan-out**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Performing preworkflow file reconnaissance**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I’ll use a bounded fan-out/synthesis triage: independent branches will inspect topology/metrics, each log chain, and cross-check red herrings; a synthesis stage will write the two required artifacts. The graph is acyclic (branches → synthesis), with completion gated by valid JSON, required fields, three file citations, and mitigation/verification steps. Direct observations must be labeled separately from inferences; no input file will be changed.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0449d91e01a5cb75016a9524212fc087d2888c442e28f8e30c\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_OdnGgOPeuUNctzJ3gYo5pDNX|fc_0449d91e01a5cb75016a9524294a4c87d2a1795ec3a00ae824","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/in/topology.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_tQZtkCCNmzVbjAuyz9SFlinX|fc_0449d91e01a5cb75016a9524294a5c87d29986a0da28b81a7a","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_gNV4B41WuOuFdkAGdN0VOhK2|fc_0449d91e01a5cb75016a9524294a6487d28c165545f7255b4e","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/072-064-service-dependency-triage-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.6-luna/oc-bench-v2-064-service-dependency-triage-gpt-5.6-luna-20260831-024956-ed4606a1/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":1704,"o